  "runtimeNotes": [
    "proper-lockfile is the only non-Vitest third-party import in the first-party runtime closure.",
    "proper-lockfile requires graceful-fs, retry, and signal-exit; the four complete resolved package trees are captured above.",
    "signal-exit registration is a module-load side effect; proper-lockfile also creates test-owned lock directories and unref'd renewal timers while a lock is held.",
    "The baseline runner binds Git-tracked first-party source and license bytes. This separate snapshot records the installed third-party closure; it does not extend the runner's receipt binding or claim a generic package sandbox."
